    <h2 class="section-title">About</h2>
    <p class="about-text">
      I grew up in Simsbury, Connecticut, and a senior-year tour of Pratt &amp; Whitney's East
      Hartford campus &mdash; standing next to jet engines &mdash; is what pushed me toward
      engineering. I'm now studying electrical engineering at McGill, where I also play flanker
      for the varsity rugby team. I'm an Eagle Scout (Troop 175, Simsbury; my Eagle Project was a
      nature-center exhibit), and in high school I ran a lawn care business and captained the
      rugby team. On campus, I volunteer on the grill at the Engineering Undergraduate Society bar
      on Fridays and was a captain for ECSE Week. I'm aiming for aerospace, with a particular pull
      toward embedded systems, firmware, and industrial automation &mdash; and outside of
      engineering, you'll find me hiking, skiing, or at a chessboard.
    </p>
